Provenance of the Nintendo 64 machine layer (runtime/guests/n64)

The register rules and timing below are ported from ares,
https://github.com/ares-emulator/ares, commit
0b928930af4cc59ed99e942996f0d3c815379388, ISC license (text below). The
code here is new C11 in relift's scheduler shape (closed forms and
scheduler events instead of per-cycle threads); each ported file keeps the
ISC notice in its header.

pi.c      the PI registers, the DMA's block shape, its duration from the
          domain timing, the busy and error rules, the bus write window
                                   n64/pi/io.cpp, dma.cpp, bus.hpp
si.c      the SI registers, the DMA durations, the bus write window
                                   n64/si/io.cpp, dma.cpp
pif.c     the joybus command block parse, run and timing estimate
                                   n64/pif/hle.cpp, io.cpp, pif.cpp
pad.c     the standard controller's answers, the pak CRC
                                   n64/controller/gamepad/gamepad.cpp
cart.c    the cartridge bus devices, the latch, the SRAM view
                                   n64/pi/bus.hpp, device.hpp,
                                   n64/cartridge/cartridge.hpp
flash.c   the Flash chip's command set, status and ID reads, timings
                                   n64/cartridge/flash.cpp
eeprom.c  the EEPROM joybus commands
                                   n64/cartridge/joybus.cpp
bus.c     the CPU's read latency of the RCP and the PI bus
                                   n64/memory/io.hpp, bus.hpp, n64/pi/bus.hpp
vi.c      the VI registers, the line counter, field and leap pattern, the
          interrupt line rules, the frame edge, the scan-out's window,
          guard band, scaling and field lines
                                   n64/vi/vi.cpp, io.cpp
ai.c      the AI registers, the DMA FIFO, the address carry, the
          interrupt at the start of each buffer, the DAC's rate and decay
                                   n64/ai/ai.cpp, io.cpp

machine.c (MI, RI, the boot words), save.c and code.c are
relift's own, written from the public n64brew documentation.

